  "title": "Free Energy Summary",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Gibbs free energy ("
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "G"
              },
              {
                "text": ") is a state function defined with regard to system quantities only and may be used to predict the spontaneity of a process. A negative value for Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "G"
              },
              {
                "text": " indicates a spontaneous process; a positive Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "G"
              },
              {
                "text": " indicates a nonspontaneous process; and a Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "G"
              },
              {
                "text": " of zero indicates that the system is at equilibrium. A number of approaches to the computation of free energy changes are possible."
              }
            ],
            "id": "08styrp5m91e9l4",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "ejvlsh59qyk9thd",
                "text": "End of Lesson Self-Assessment"
              }
            ],
            "id": "qswfskxqjwmq98a",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Before you take the quiz, please evaluate your understanding of the learning objectives for the module "
